<h2 id="deploying-the-application" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Deploying the application</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#deploying-the-application" aria-label="Link to Deploying the application"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>When you’re ready to deploy your Next.js application, you can use any platform that supports Next.js, such as Vercel, Netlify or VPS providers. Be sure to configure the required environment variables (<code>DATABASE_URL</code>, <code>NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL</code>, and <code>NEON_AUTH_COOKIE_SECRET</code>) in your deployment settings.</p>
<p>After deployment, add your production URLs to the <strong>Your trusted domains</strong> section in the Neon Auth settings to ensure authentication functions correctly.</p>
<h2 id="conclusion" class="anchor-heading group relative w-fit scroll-mt-20 leading-tight font-medium lg:scroll-mt-5 tracking-tighter"><span>Conclusion</span><a class="rounded-full px-2 no-underline opacity-0 transition-opacity duration-200 group-hover:opacity-100 hover:border-none hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 focus-visible:outline-offset-0 sm:hidden" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Link to Conclusion"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 14 14" class="inline text-green-44 dark:text-green-52 w-3.5"><path stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="square" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="1.4" d="m3.938 12.688 1.75-11.375M8.313 12.688l1.75-11.375M3.063 4.813h8.75M2.188 9.188h8.75"></path></svg></a></h2>
<p>In this guide, you built a secure Todo application using Next.js, Neon Auth, and Drizzle ORM. You learned how to configure Neon Auth for user authentication, define your database schema with Drizzle ORM, and use Server Actions to securely handle authentication and database operations.</p>
<p>With this foundation, you can create applications that require secure user authentication and data management using Neon Auth and Next.js.</p>
<p>Before deploying to production, be sure to review the <a class="" href="/docs/auth/production-checklist">Neon Auth production checklist</a>.</p>
